@@ -284,3 +284,33 @@ This adapter is developed and maintained by [Rui Yang](mailto:ypyangrui@pku.edu.
 * Parity logs PR (HuggingFace): https://huggingface.co/datasets/harborframework/parity-experiments/discussions/36
 * Dataset registry PR: https://github.com/laude-institute/harbor-datasets/pull/60
 * Adapter PR: https://github.com/laude-institute/harbor/pull/351, https://github.com/harbor-framework/harbor/pull/1289
+
+
+## Opt-in verifyit source runtime
+
+Add `--verifyit` when generating tasks, or pass `verifyit_enabled=True` to
+`QCircuitBenchAdapter`. The default verifier remains unchanged. The opt-in path
+runs the retained generated Python verifier through ScriptSpec in a separate
+image, using the original conda environment and Python 3.10.9. Verifyit itself
+runs in the image's separate base-Python environment (Python >=3.11).
+
+Candidate lookup preserves `/app/solution.py`, `/solution/solution.py`, then
+`/home/agent/workspace/solution.py` precedence. The source check_model dispatch,
+QASM processing, Python postprocessing, simulations, sampling and seed defaults
+remain unchanged. The semantic score keeps the source finite normalization;
+projected syntax and inverse gate-count metrics are also retained. Verdict
+metadata records all six native channels, including shot and timing ratios.
+Native auxiliary NaNs become JSON null with a raw witness and an explanation.
+A nonfinite semantic score is an infrastructure error before source clamping.
+
+Missing candidates and source-recognized candidate syntax/load errors score
+zero. Missing trusted assets, unavailable dependencies and unhandled native
+checker failures produce `infra_error` at minimum zero; malformed reference
+metadata or changed trusted QASM produces `invalid_task` at minimum zero.
+Candidate Python executes inside the retained grader runtime.
+
+Validation covers the full 28-algorithm source subset with bounded CPU source
+runs and Harbor Trials. Timing ratios are recorded separately from score parity;
+they are measured wall-clock values. Source-contract fixtures do not establish
+archived model parity or security isolation. The integration requires Harbor's
+shared `verifyit_source_runtime` helper and its pinned verifyit revision.
